.TE
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS PRAGMA_PACK_PUSH
Begins a structure packing scope by pushing the current alignment and
setting packed alignment for subsequent declarations.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
PRAGMA_PACK_PUSH
\f[B]struct\f[R] test
{
\&...
.EE
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS PRAGMA_PACK_POP
Ends a structure packing scope by restoring the previous alignment
pushed by \f[CR]PRAGMA_PACK_PUSH\f[R].
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
\&...
};
PRAGMA_PACK_POP
.EE
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS PACK
Applies the packed attribute to a structure declaration, forcing minimal
alignment and preventing padding within the structure.
.PP
Must be used inside a \f[CR]PRAGMA_PACK_PUSH\f[R] /
\f[CR]PRAGMA_PACK_POP\f[R] scope.
.PP
\f[B]Examples\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
PRAGMA_PACK_PUSH
\f[B]struct\f[R] test
{
    . . .
} PACK;
PRAGMA_PACK_POP
.EE
.IP
.EX
PRAGMA_PACK_PUSH
\f[B]typedef\f[R] \f[B]struct\f[R] test
{
    . . .
} PACK t_test;
PRAGMA_PACK_POP
.EE
